Falsifies `system_tests::user::std_threads_tests::the_std_heap_is_measured_under_four_threads`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect, in milestone 561 (a per-CPU allocator is what the current-CPU page was for): a thread's
end closes its allocation cache but never gives the blocks back to the heap. Each ended thread
then keeps up to 34,816 bytes for good, and `std_heap_contention`'s 64 cache-filling threads spend
twice its one-mebibyte budget, so the program aborts out of memory before its last line.

Expected to fail: "std_heap_contention ended before its output did".

diff --git a/patches/std-nife/overlay/std/src/sys/thread_local/key/nife.rs b/patches/std-nife/overlay/std/src/sys/thread_local/key/nife.rs
--- a/patches/std-nife/overlay/std/src/sys/thread_local/key/nife.rs
+++ b/patches/std-nife/overlay/std/src/sys/thread_local/key/nife.rs
@@ -312,7 +312,6 @@
     // after it go to the heap rather than refilling the cache.
     unsafe {
         (*b).cache_closed = true;
-        crate::sys::alloc::nife::spill_thread_cache(&mut (*b).cache);
     }
 }
 
